  "summary": "On 1 December 1959 twelve countries whose scientists had worked in Antarctica during the International Geophysical Year signed the Antarctic Treaty in Washington. It reserves the continent for peaceful purposes, keeps scientific research free and its results shared, and sets territorial claims aside. It entered into force in 1961.",
